+# [2026-10-22] Admission worker lease must include inference and idle time
+
+- Symptom: a worker that finishes its waiting phase can lose its admission lease while inference continues or between requests.
+- Root cause: the first client draft stopped its wait task when the local pending map became empty.
+- Why: queue waiting ownership and worker process lifetime were incorrectly conflated.
+- Fix: keep one bounded long-poll heartbeat from capability hello until client close; collect errors and fail subsequent allocations after a hub fault.
+- Test interception: parent repository `test_client_lost_enqueue_ack_idle_heartbeat_and_cancellation` waits beyond a worker lease then allocates again; the lease remains valid. Real Motor ZMQ multi-worker/cross-process coverage checks the shared broker path.
+- Scenario: enforce/shadow worker with no queued request but a long-running P/D request or idle gap.
+- Keywords: admission, worker lease, heartbeat, idle, lifecycle.
